Context
  Asked to run against all ../guile-* projects and check whether correct Emacs,
  debugger, Geiser and REPL support is available, with guile-sage called out as the
  large case.

Deviations
  Read-only by design. Starting 34 REPLs to test them would have created exactly the
  orphan problem this repository documents, and readiness is answerable by looking.

Considerations
  gdb is not part of the sweep. It was checked separately and is built --without-guile
  here, so the GDB-scriptable-in-Guile path is unavailable on this cell regardless of
  project -- that is a cell property, not a per-project one, and it belongs in the
  channels experiment where it was measured.

  guile-sage is the largest checkout at 119 MB and the detector handles it without
  special-casing: modules under src/ in the (sage ...) namespace, tests/ with SRFI-64,
  load path -L src -L tests. Nothing about scale broke it.

Timeline
  2026-09-29, nexus, as dsp-dr. 34 checkouts, 66 derived ports, 2 collisions, 1
  detector bug found and fixed by running it.
